[assistant] All tests pass now — **768 passed, 21202 subtests passed, exit code 0**.

I made four independent minimal fixes, each in `more_itertools/` (no test files touched, no new deps):

1. **`more.py:244` (chunked strict)** — root cause was the divisibility check `if len(chunk) > n`. A final short chunk has length *less* than `n`, never greater, so it was never rejected. Fixed to `!= n`, which raises `ValueError` for any non-full final chunk. (This was the failure behind `test_strict_being_true`.)

2. **`more.py:1068` (windowed padding)** — the padding was computed as `(fillvalue,) * (n - len(window) + 1)`, an off-by-one that emitted one *extra* fillvalue. Removed the `+ 1` so a short first window is padded exactly to width `n`. (Fixed both `test_basic` n=6 and `test_fillvalue`.)

3. **`recipes.py:163` (tail, sized path)** — the start index was `max(0, size - n + 1)`, one *too far*, dropping an extra leading element (e.g. `tail(3,'ABCDEFG')` returned `['F','G']`). Removed the `+ 1` → `max(0, size - n)`. (Fixed `test_sized_equal` and `test_sized_greater`.)

4. **`recipes.py:931` (sieve)** — the guard was `if n >= 2: yield 2`, but the contract is "primes **less than** n", so for `n=2` it wrongly yielded `[2]`. Changed to `if n > 2: yield 2`; negative inputs still raise `ValueError` via `isqrt`. (Fixed `test_small_numbers`.)

Net effect: 6 failures traced to 4 distinct one-token defects (two `+1` off-by-ones, one comparison operator, one boundary condition).

